status: open

---

Generalize ticket statuses.

Currently the recognized options are "open" and "closed", but this is rigid and goes against the
philosophy of this project. The statuses should be generalized and the tools updated to
accommodate.


CLI:

The CLI currently has "close" and "reopen" options. This needs to change to a general option. One
idea is to have a "get" and "set" command which works like this:

    ticket get 123 status
    ticket set 123 status:closed
    ticket clear 123 status

This way, the commands are generalized across all metadata tags which will allow things like this:

    ticket set 123 "assignee:David Reid"

When a "get" command is used but the metadata key does not exist, it should still return success,
but output nothing.

The "set" command should create the metadata tag if it does not exist. It should also allow
changing of multiple tags in a single command:

    ticket set 123 status:review "assignee:David Reid"

When setting metadata, there is a special case for the status. In this case, it will by default
insert a message saying "Status changed from [old status] to [new status]". If there is no old
status, there should be no message. Clearing a status should not add a message. Setting a status
to its current value should succeed without changing the ticket or adding a message.

The "clear" command will delete the metadata item. Multiple metadata items can be passed in
exactly like "set":

    ticket clear 123 status assignee

The "set" and "clear" commands should honour the "--no-comment" option.

Metadata arguments for "set" should be split at the first colon so values can contain additional
colons. Keys and values must not be empty. A command must not contain the same key more than once.
Metadata changes should be atomic. If one argument is invalid, no metadata must change.

The "close" and "reopen" commands would become aliases for the time being for backwards
compatibility and should keep their current behaviour. They should be removed from usage
instructions and all documentation to discourage use.


VS Code:

The VS Code extension should allow users to configure groups which map to a status. The default
configuration should contain the current Open and Closed groups with their current expanded
states. Group order should follow the order in the configuration. Each group should have a label,
status, and initial collapsed state. For example:

    {
        "label": "Open",
        "status": "open",
        "expanded": true
    }

The configuration should work in user and workspace settings. A workspace setting should replace
the complete user group list instead of merging with it.
Changes to group or initial-status configuration should refresh the ticket tree automatically.

There should be a permanent Uncategorized group as a fallback for tickets which have no status or
have a status that does not map to a configured group. Duplicate status mappings should be treated
as an invalid configuration and reported to the user.

The right-click menu should have a "Set Status..." command. The command should open a selection
list which contains all configured statuses. A dynamic context menu or sub-menu should not be used
because VS Code menu contributions are static.

Since the status is now generalized, there should be a configuration option for the initial status.
It should default to "open". If the configuration has an empty string, new tickets should not have
status metadata.


